WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:04.730
Welcome to "Ear Biscuits,"

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:06.470
the podcast where two lifelong friends

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:08.100
talk about life for a long time.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.060
I'm Rhett.

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:10.050
And I'm Link.

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:13.160
This week at the round
table of dim lighting,

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:15.880
we're gonna talk about some

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:19.256
of your most embarrassing
holiday memories.

00:00:19.256 --> 00:00:21.330
'Cause we thought, you know what?

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:24.600
The holidays are strange
this year and strained.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:26.840
I mean, a lot of plans
that have been altered

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:28.380
or canceled altogether.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.440
I mean, as we've discussed,

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:33.898
neither one of us are
going home for the holidays

00:00:33.898 --> 00:00:38.703
because of the pandemic
and all the unknowns.

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:44.906
And so we're sitting here in
this weird holiday experience,

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:47.460
different from any we've ever had.

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:50.370
And I just thought it would be fun

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:54.470
to talk about embarrassing things

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:55.890
that have happened over the holidays

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:57.490
so then we could at least say,

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:58.420
if you're not going home,

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:00.140
if you're not seeing your loved ones,

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:01.060
you could at least be like,

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:03.030
well, at least the chances

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:04.790
of something that embarrassing happening

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:06.170
have gone down drastically.

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:07.974
Well, I mean, I don't know.

00:01:07.974 --> 00:01:12.284
I can embarrass myself in front
of my own immediate family.

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:15.760
I guess it is harder to do though.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:19.533
Especially, depending on what
kind of family you go home to,

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:24.360
like, if you are like a new spouse,

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:26.365
which we've got a couple
of those situations,

00:01:26.365 --> 00:01:31.365
going home for Christmas
with your new spouse

00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:34.780
for the first time,

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:36.760
or you're just like a
new boyfriend/girlfriend

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:37.593
kind of thing.

00:01:37.593 --> 00:01:38.426
I think that's where

00:01:38.426 --> 00:01:40.960
there's the most potential
for embarrassment.

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:43.690
'Cause you're entering
into an unknown situation

00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:45.567
and you don't know how
they're gonna treat you,

00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:47.680
don't know what kind of
things they're gonna say.

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:50.567
I mean, what kind of environment
are you walking into?

00:01:50.567 --> 00:01:52.230
Are you gonna say the wrong thing?

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:53.700
Are you gonna look at
somebody the wrong way?

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:57.840
Are you not gonna understand Uncle Barry?

00:01:57.840 --> 00:01:58.673
Uncle Barry.

00:01:58.673 --> 00:02:01.090
You know, you don't have to
worry about that this year.

00:02:01.090 --> 00:02:03.440
Yeah, that's so long ago for us.

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:08.440
I can barely remember
just getting to know,

00:02:09.010 --> 00:02:11.000
like before they were my in-laws,

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:15.907
like going in on Christmas
with them or whatever.

00:02:15.907 --> 00:02:16.740
Me especially.
But it was

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:17.573
a high pressure situation.

00:02:17.573 --> 00:02:18.960
But you too.

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:23.180
I had a whole lot of interaction
with my wife's family,

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:26.600
even before we started dating, really,

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:28.950
because that's how I got to know Jessie

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:31.180
was by knowing her family first.

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:32.933
So it was a little bit less of a,

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:35.283
and definitely by the
time we were married,

00:02:35.283 --> 00:02:36.200
it was like.
It wasn't pressurized.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:41.200
Yes, actually we lived above their garage.

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:44.370
That's right.
In that little one bedroom

00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:49.570
with a slanting roof that I had to duck

00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:51.052
just to walk around up there.

00:02:51.052 --> 00:02:54.453
We grew up around our
families, like whenever,

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:58.170
Christy started being
introduced to my family.

00:02:58.170 --> 00:03:00.600
It was like, that was
more of a dating thing

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:01.470
than a holiday thing,

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:04.450
because we all lived in
relatively the same area,

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:05.690
but for other people, yeah.

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:09.150
It's like introducing someone
to your significant other

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:12.300
for the first time happens
a lot around the holidays.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:14.200
We also weren't.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:18.280
I mean, as different
as your family might be

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:19.240
from your wife's family,

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:22.030
or my family might be
from my wife's family,

00:03:22.030 --> 00:03:24.440
we're still all a bunch of
people from North Carolina.

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:26.550
Like, it's not like you're going

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:28.560
to a whole different culture
or something like that.

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:29.393
So it was like,

00:03:29.393 --> 00:03:31.920
I kinda know what I'm getting
myself into here, right?

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:34.600
Well, before we get into
those stories though,

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:38.420
I have an embarrassing story
that I already told you,

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:39.960
but now I'm gonna tell everybody.

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:42.480
Everybody needs to hear this.

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:44.030
It's not embarrassing for me.

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:48.700
It's not really a holiday
story either, but.

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:52.875
It felt a little embarrassed

00:03:52.875 --> 00:03:55.920
when you share the full
extent of it with me.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:56.763
Okay. Well.

00:03:57.660 --> 00:03:58.873
But let them have it.

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:03.253
Yesterday, as a matter
of fact, this happened.

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:07.083
We're recording this on
a Monday and yesterday,

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:10.410
I took the boys, my two sons,

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:12.070
Locke and Shepherd on a Sunday drive.

00:04:12.070 --> 00:04:14.510
Now, you've been doing
some family driving,

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:16.170
and you've talked about
that during the pandemic.

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:18.990
Early on in quarantine, it
was like, you know what?

00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:20.300
We're just gonna drive around.

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:22.640
We're gonna see what's
happening or not happening,

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:23.790
but we're not gonna get out of the car.

00:04:23.790 --> 00:04:25.990
We're gonna stay in the safety of our car.

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:28.340
That kind of trickled off after a while.

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:30.530
And I was just like,
I'm gonna take the boys,

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:32.330
kind of get them out.

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:35.857
And, you know, there was
like, talk of going surfing.

00:04:35.857 --> 00:04:37.665
Trickled off is a little
foreshadowing for you.

00:04:37.665 --> 00:04:40.120
We were talking about maybe
like going to the beach

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:42.640
or going surfing, but we're
like, what if we just drove?

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:45.040
And we stopped at a bunch
of places and, you know,

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:48.020
we've got one of the most famous drives

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:51.530
that you can do in the
entire world is the PCH.

00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:52.450
And it's right here.

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:53.400
We can just get on it.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:56.110
The Pacific Coast Highway
is what that stands for.

00:04:56.110 --> 00:04:58.620
This is the highway that
goes right up the coast.

00:04:58.620 --> 00:04:59.453
The one.

00:04:59.453 --> 00:05:03.760
I had never eaten at this
place called Neptune's Net,

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:05.800
which is the place-
I haven't either.

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:09.620
It's pretty far North.
It's County Line Beach.

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:11.740
So all the way at the County line between-

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:13.240
Oh, above Malibu.

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:14.870
Yeah. I mean, like, if you're-

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:16.686
Oh, you went way up there.

00:05:16.686 --> 00:05:17.519
Well, that was the whole idea.

00:05:17.519 --> 00:05:19.450
We were gonna drive all the way to Oxnard.

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:22.084
See what Oxnard's all about.

00:05:22.084 --> 00:05:24.880
You know, it's kind of a weird name.

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:27.720
And I've always kinda
been interested in, like,

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:29.431
what's going over here,

00:05:29.431 --> 00:05:32.120
what's on what's happening
in Oxnard and Ventura,

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:33.820
but we never make it out that way.

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:39.990
And I had had intentions
of eating at Neptune's Net,

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:42.783
for some time, but of course, you know,

00:05:42.783 --> 00:05:46.690
with COVID and everything,
wasn't making my way down there,

00:05:46.690 --> 00:05:49.890
but I go online and there's
like a drive-through situation.

00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:51.590
And let me tell you,

00:05:51.590 --> 00:05:53.680
not that Neptune's Net
needs any more business,

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:55.870
because it was, it was very busy,

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:58.700
but they have it figured out.

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:01.270
What do you mean? Is it
like a fried seafood place?

00:06:01.270 --> 00:06:03.540
I think that they are probably most known

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:07.407
for their fried seafood, but
they also have grilled seafood.

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:12.850
Fish tacos, hamburgers, lots of things.

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:15.270
But they got the drive-thru
COVID thing figured out?

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:17.290
Very well. They have some outdoor seating,

00:06:17.290 --> 00:06:18.410
which we didn't do. We were just like,

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:20.230
we're gonna do the drive-through
thing and maybe like eat

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:24.020
in the car, you know, safety first.

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:26.220
I'm always on the fence
about fish and chips

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:27.720
I don't want to talk about fish and chips.

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:28.830
I want to talk about what happened.

00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:31.830
I know, but I gotta say this
though, I gotta say this man.

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:36.320
They got- if you have are on
the fence about fish and chips

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:38.853
like I was, this will
completely redeem it.

00:06:41.445 --> 00:06:44.577
So that was our first stop
driving all the way up Malibu.

00:06:45.940 --> 00:06:50.040
And we stop at Neptune's Net,
go through the drive through,

00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:52.280
get our food, eat it in the car.

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:53.290
And then we're like, alright,

00:06:53.290 --> 00:06:56.343
let's take a little
stroll down to the beach.

00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:59.860
Let's go down to the beach and okay.

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:02.620
I'm premising this with letting you know,

00:07:02.620 --> 00:07:05.590
I'm not a braggy daddy, but I own a Tesla.

00:07:05.590 --> 00:07:06.730
That is the car that I drive.

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:08.960
If you remember The Society,
you've seen me drive it

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:11.060
in some of the carpool vlogs.

00:07:11.060 --> 00:07:13.990
But I have to say that by
way of setting the context

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:15.903
for why what happened, happened.

00:07:19.776 --> 00:07:22.440
So Tesla has this thing
called sentry mode,

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:25.620
which is, there's cameras on the car,

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:29.440
and you can have it set so
that when you leave the car

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:30.810
and it knows you left the car

00:07:30.810 --> 00:07:32.917
because your phone is the
key to the car, right?

00:07:32.917 --> 00:07:35.580
And so when you get away,
you walk away from the car,

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:38.960
the car locks and it automatically
goes into sentry mode,

00:07:38.960 --> 00:07:41.790
which is it is recording everything

00:07:41.790 --> 00:07:44.490
that is happening around your car.

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:45.830
So if somebody comes up and-

00:07:45.830 --> 00:07:48.900
All the cameras that are
used to help it navigate

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:51.108
and know, Oh, you're passing a pedestrian

00:07:51.108 --> 00:07:54.180
or another car is in your blind spot.

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:55.570
Or like when you drive your car,

00:07:55.570 --> 00:07:58.345
it shows trash cans on
the side of the road.

00:07:58.345 --> 00:07:59.670
I actually don't think
that that's using it.

00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:00.820
I think it's using the cameras

00:08:00.820 --> 00:08:03.080
and maybe like some sort
of LIDAR or something.

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:05.520
Okay. But the camera's
everywhere for like-

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:07.306
Backing up and maneuvering it.

00:08:07.306 --> 00:08:09.020
But they're constantly recording.

00:08:09.020 --> 00:08:10.750
There's a camera in the front,

00:08:10.750 --> 00:08:13.533
camera in the back and then
two cameras on the sides.

00:08:15.497 --> 00:08:19.010
And so what it'll do, if
somebody comes up to the car,

00:08:19.010 --> 00:08:21.000
it actually, if you get close to the car,

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:22.250
when it's in sentry mode,

00:08:23.180 --> 00:08:24.860
if you happen to look inside the car

00:08:24.860 --> 00:08:28.420
and you see this big screen,
it'll say "sentry mode,

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:30.180
you are being recorded"
or something like that.

00:08:30.180 --> 00:08:32.150
Like it lets you know, so
people who are like trying

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:33.820
to break in, "Oh, crap,
I'm being recorded."

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:36.570
And you have to hook a
hard drive up to your car.

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:39.148
Like a little USB hard drive
is like in the console.

00:08:39.148 --> 00:08:41.810
So then when you come back to the car,

00:08:41.810 --> 00:08:44.950
it says "14 sentry mode events recorded,"

00:08:44.950 --> 00:08:48.333
and then you go and you
watch them, if you so please,

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:51.700
So we're walking on the beach

00:08:51.700 --> 00:08:54.048
and I get an alert on my phone,

00:08:54.048 --> 00:08:57.690
"sentry recording initiated'
or something like that.

00:08:57.690 --> 00:08:58.523
Uh oh.

00:08:58.523 --> 00:09:02.590
And then it was like
"car alarm initiated,"

00:09:02.590 --> 00:09:04.950
which has never happened, you know?

00:09:04.950 --> 00:09:06.050
In the whole time I've owned the car.

00:09:06.050 --> 00:09:07.670
Could you stop it?

00:09:07.670 --> 00:09:10.270
Or what did you do? Did
you run back to the car?

00:09:10.270 --> 00:09:11.500
No. Cause I was like,

00:09:11.500 --> 00:09:12.793
this is probably just-

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:15.660
you can't like look into that.

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:17.020
It's not like a Nest
cam where you can like,

00:09:17.020 --> 00:09:20.470
look and see what the car is
recording from your phone.

00:09:20.470 --> 00:09:22.040
I was just like, this is
probably one of those-

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:24.546
There's so many motorcycles on the PCH

00:09:24.546 --> 00:09:26.700
and lots of loud
motorcycles. And I was like,

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:28.550
this is probably just a
loud motorcycle going by

00:09:28.550 --> 00:09:30.600
and setting the alarm off.

00:09:30.600 --> 00:09:33.880
Cause I had seen so many, so I didn't-

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:34.960
we kept walking around.

00:09:34.960 --> 00:09:36.560
And then we'd go back to the car

00:09:42.304 --> 00:09:43.137
and you can bring up the files,

00:09:43.137 --> 00:09:46.070
and there's a little red
dot on the, you know,

00:09:46.070 --> 00:09:48.910
you can scroll to the red dot
to see what the event was.

00:09:48.910 --> 00:09:51.680
And so we just like, okay,
there's like 15 events recorded.

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:55.050
I'm like, let's see what
set the car alarm off.

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:57.740
And we were kind of doing it
just to have fun, you know,

00:09:57.740 --> 00:09:59.590
showing the boys like how this works.

00:10:00.670 --> 00:10:02.540
And so we kind of go through,

00:10:02.540 --> 00:10:04.910
most of it is just people
walking past the car

00:10:06.637 --> 00:10:09.970
is what set the little
red dot off. And then, Oh,

00:10:09.970 --> 00:10:11.710
here's where the car
alarm went off. Oh yes.

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:13.923
It was a giant Harley that went by,

00:10:14.998 --> 00:10:16.530
like just set it off, you know?

00:10:16.530 --> 00:10:17.363
Wow.

00:10:17.363 --> 00:10:20.580
But then there's this other
event and we scroll to it

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:22.550
and, now this is giving me an idea.

00:10:22.550 --> 00:10:27.550
The camera, it's like the camera
is in the rear view mirror

00:10:28.470 --> 00:10:32.453
and it's showing you like
the length of the car.

00:10:33.310 --> 00:10:36.463
I would call it a blind spot mirror.

00:10:37.971 --> 00:10:41.620
Like it's shooting like past the car

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:42.630
where a car would be in your blind spot.

00:10:42.630 --> 00:10:46.300
So if someone comes and
stands next to your car,

00:10:46.300 --> 00:10:48.380
you see their entire body.

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:50.530
But the camera is really
kind of focused right

00:10:50.530 --> 00:10:53.240
on their midsection, which is important.

00:10:53.240 --> 00:10:55.180
Yeah. Or like where,

00:10:55.180 --> 00:10:57.890
where you would aim a
camera if someone were

00:10:57.890 --> 00:10:59.040
in a car driving.

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:00.190
In the middle of the body.

00:11:00.190 --> 00:11:01.830
Car level.

00:11:01.830 --> 00:11:03.880
Now, in addition to people on motorcycles,

00:11:03.880 --> 00:11:06.450
there's lots of people on bicycles.

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:09.383
And we say, Oh, there's an older man.

00:11:10.850 --> 00:11:13.550
You know, who's been riding
a bicycle, he's got the full,

00:11:13.550 --> 00:11:16.900
like bike gear on and the helmet.

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:20.100
And he walks right up to our car,

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:24.133
looks over his shoulder
and then whips it out.

00:11:25.100 --> 00:11:27.233
And by "it", I mean his penis.

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:31.070
Why do you gotta say it like that?

00:11:31.070 --> 00:11:32.880
Wiener man. Say his Wiener,

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:33.713
His Wiener.

00:11:35.860 --> 00:11:37.733
And proceeds to urinate.

00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:41.873
And it's one of those things.

00:11:41.873 --> 00:11:43.843
That once you start seeing
it, you can't, it's not like,

00:11:43.843 --> 00:11:45.010
I mean, we just,

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:49.080
me and the boys just start
laughing hysterically

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:50.280
Well, let me tell you.

